If you use the results, the thing worth citing is not the numbers but the three
measurement defects described in README.md -- a reaper queue that put the
youngest creature first in line to die, a classifier that counted any successful
division as reproduction, and a cost measured with one creature alone in an
empty dish. Each of them silently shaped results before it was found.
